@startuml View the Version and the License Notice

actor User
actor Backend
participant Frontend

note left of User
  Backend is in operation, or it gives an error response.
  User has a web browser and the address of the page.
end note

User -> Frontend: User opens the page of the application in the browser.
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the waiting message for the information of the service.
Frontend -> Backend: Frontend sends the request GET /info to Backend.
Backend -> Frontend: Backend sends the response with the version, the commit, the copyright holder, the address of the repository and the license to Frontend.
alt Backend sends an error response
Backend -> Frontend: Backend sends the error response with the error code and the trace identifier to Frontend.
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the heading that the information is not available, the text for the error code, and the trace identifier.
note right
  The text is in the language of the page. Frontend does not show the members title and detail of the error response.
end note
end
alt Backend gives no response
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the heading that the information is not available and the text that the service gives no response.
note right
  There is no trace identifier in this case.
end note
end
alt Backend sends a response that Frontend cannot read
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the heading that the information is not available and the text that the response of the service is not valid.
note right
  There is no trace identifier in this case.
end note
end
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the notice of the license at the bottom of the page, in the language of the page.
note right
  Step 4: Frontend shows the notice as
  English: Copyright 2026 Ronald Rink, https://github.com/dfch/biz.dfch.SpecMgrDemo. Licensed under AGPL-3.0-only.
  German: Copyright 2026 Ronald Rink, https://github.com/dfch/biz.dfch.SpecMgrDemo. Lizenziert unter AGPL-3.0-only.
end note
Frontend -> User: Frontend shows User the version and the commit of the build, in the language of the page.
note right
  Step 5: Frontend shows the version as
  English: Version {version}, commit {commit}
  German: Version {version}, Commit {commit}
end note
User -> User: User reads the notice of the license, the version and the commit.

note left of User
  The page shows the notice of the license (the copyright holder, the address of the repository and the license).
  The page shows the version and the commit of the build.
end note
note left of User
  The page shows the heading that the information is not available, and the text for the cause.
  The page shows no notice, no version and no commit.
end note
@enduml
